function tbl = blerTable()
%blerTable Measured PSSCH and PSCCH block error rates. GENERATED -- do not hand-edit.
%Spec:   none. This is measurement output, produced by +harness/+lls/blerSweep over the real
%        transmit chains (phy.chan.pscchTx/psschTx), a real OFDM waveform, DM-RS channel
%        estimation and zero-forcing equalisation, with soft combining across redundancy
%        versions. Regenerate with harness.lls.blerSweep and re-emit; never edit the numbers.
%Inputs: none
%Outputs: tbl  scalar struct: .mcs .snrDb .attempt (axes), .pssch (nMcs x nSnr x nAttempt),
%              .pscch (nMcs x nSnr), .meta (the conditions it was measured under)
%
%WHAT THIS TABLE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER
%----------------------------------------
%Measured over TDL-D at 120 km/h, one allocation width and one receiver configuration; the
%exact values are in .meta. harness.phyabs.blerLookup REJECTS a lookup at any other channel
%model or speed rather than answering with these curves, because silently reading a table
%off-key is indistinguishable from having measured the right one. Another channel is a new
%measurement, not a reinterpretation of this one.
%
%The receiver was NOT given the channel or the noise variance -- both are estimated from the
%DM-RS. These curves therefore sit to the right of a perfect-CSI measurement, which is the
%honest number rather than the flattering one.
%
%A faded waterfall is BROAD -- tens of measured points span the transition where AWGN takes
%two or three -- and it is not perfectly monotone, because each point is 60 Monte Carlo
%trials and 1/60 is the finest error rate it can resolve. The numbers are emitted raw: no
%smoothing, no monotonicity enforcement, nothing between the measurement and the table.

